jobs.description:
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Business Development Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a Nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Business Development Associates bring ideas, initiatives, and activities that help grow our business day in and day out. They join, support, and collaborate with teams focused on specific opportunities, ensuring that the pursuit of new business is rigorous, disciplined, and ethical. They collaborate closely to craft strategies and plans and set the standard for creative excellence in business development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IDEO London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a global design consultancy where curiosity, empathy, and solving complex challenges drive us. For over 40 years, we&#39;ve partnered with clients to innovate in healthcare, mobility, education, retail, and beyond. Here, every challenge is a chance to grow, connect, and create impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why is this role important for IDEO&#39;s work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Development is at the heart of connecting IDEO&#39;s creative capabilities with the people and organisations who need them. It&#39;s about more than winning new work. It&#39;s about understanding our clients&#39; challenges, building trusted relationships, and helping shape opportunities where human-centred design can make a meaningful difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Once Here You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize your time to collaborate and support the London Studio in landing project work - with new and returning clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an IDEO ambassador and be the first touch point for new potential clients, ensuring a positive initial experience with IDEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage opportunity qualification, owning continuity of the BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involve internal leadership and designers as needed for boosts and to help determine strategic fit, frame opportunities, scope programs and articulate next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull in director-level support as needed for advocating for client needs and negotiation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finalize pitch decks, learn the industries of our client leads by conducting research and editing proposal decks, and brainstorm client deliverable options and consulting solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct client due diligence to help BD teams get smart and prepare for calls, creating intelligent discussion guides that help us start to build a relationship with potential clients from Day One.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and communicate market trends and themes to teams on a monthly basis that can be used to help shape our thinking and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REPORTING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track quarterly goals pertaining to recognized revenue, monthly profit and yield marks, time to close, conversion rate, qualification rate, and win rate KPIs within the London Hub. Report back in the pipeline meetings, looking for ways to engage the team in the information and how they need to apply it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be familiar with metrics that point towards the health of the business and be able to assist with ad-hoc reporting needs as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare a monthly summary of insights and thought leadership (from IDEO and beyond), including how it applies to day-to-day business, to share with key clients as a value add.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DATA INTEGRITY&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Director/Enterprise team to ensure the CRM system is kept up to date, including our pipeline and pre-pipeline in Hubspot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that relevant documents related to BD are being stored and filed accordingly in the BD section of Google Drive (not on personal drives or Slack!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appropriately loop in Legal, Marketing, Finance, and other functions as needed to progress an ongoing BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain lists in Hubspot and LinkedIn Sales Navigator: who are our key clients, our lapsed clients, our warm contacts, the cold contacts we want to reach? Who’s engaging with our newsletters, with our LinkedIn, etc? Provide recommendations on how we might reach out to these folks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROGRAM MANAGEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise project management tactical skills by effectively steering the BD process for new and existing work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and take action on the business development process and client needs based on what we’re hearing and seeing in the pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate meetings with potential leads, ensure prompt and adequate follow-ups, manage legal agreement workflows, coordinate proposal research across teams, and ensure continual progress to meet client deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team balance meeting the needs of existing clientele with prioritizing time for proactive outreach to land new clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and project manage lead generation activities, such as BD-specific mailers to LON Hub mailing lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account planning activities to drive a proactive, consistent approach to client investment and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment of the right expertise and experience from within the hub team towards client pursuits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMMUNICATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate persuasive and effective communication and presentation skills along with the confidence to command a room for the client and network-building meetings or events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to providing excellent team and client communication and collaboration that shows an understanding of leading with empathy, openness, and curiosity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower other team members to consistently gather and share inspiration, work, and learnings with teams and clients. This should come through leading by example as well as having a knowledge management system where folks can exchange and store content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen existing assets and develop new ones in collaboration with subject matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with LON Hub Marketing to stay abreast of competitors and any impact that industry and economic changes and movements might have on our go to market positioning and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NETWORK BUILDING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate knowledge of the different approaches across each of our three offer sets, and understand the different areas of expertise of our design disciplines to confidently speak to our capabilities in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build cross-discipline relationships across IDEO in order to effectively help generate and capture written, verbal and visual input from IDEO leadership and design teams to potential client leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate your internal networks as well as you professional networks virtually on social media channels and live at education and industry-related associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support top-of-funnel growth activity including working with the Executive Director of Growth, Marketing and portfolio teams to translate targeting priorities into actionable prospect audiences and lists for campaigns, events, roadshows and other market-facing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPLORE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen your foundational BD skills and capabilities, using your learning budget intentionally to build on growth opportunities identified with your business lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain an understanding of GenAI and how it can support and improve the BD process, from generating client intelligence to scoring our RFP responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support special projects as needed and provide support on other processes and projects outside the immediate area of responsibilities as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with internal programs and initiatives to improve organizational BD efforts, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active member of the London community, coming into the office as needed, playing a role in our core rituals, such as Tuesday Morning Meetings, participating in SASU, and attending Hub gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3-5 years of relevant experience in client relationship management and business development, preferably within a creative environment and/or design consultancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills with proven ability to prioritize tasks, keep momentum and develop timelines, involve and engage stakeholders, and maintain empathy for both internal and client teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to create and deliver presentations, proposals, and other assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data literacy: fluent in G-suite (slides, docs, and sheets), Workday, CRM, and translating quantitative outputs into actionable qualitative insights for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and communication skills to effectively and efficiently bridge between IDEO and its clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct and synthesize research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to Detail: Demonstrates concern for the details and their impact on the larger picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a wide range of market analysis tools, data sets, and benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort determining next steps in ambiguous situations with limited direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to pitch in on tasks, big or small. Volunteer and helper mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to collaborate across various design disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take chances without being afraid to fail and learn along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insatiable curiosity to learn more about businesses, industries, markets, and what drives them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MINDSET&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground in Self-Awareness: Reflect on your biases and lenses to be more inclusive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show Curiosity: Question accepted norms to make room to learn from more diverse voices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean into Vulnerability: Build trust by being open.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask for and give consistent and timely feedback on personal performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be optimistic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embrace ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk Less, Do more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make others successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does IDEO offer you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation and creativity:&lt;/strong&gt; Dive into a variety of projects from creating breakthrough digital products and experiences, to designing new customer interactions, to building innovation capabilities – working alongside talented individuals across disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether it’s strengthening your project leadership, deepening your interaction design craft or exploring new technologies, we’re here to support your journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community and well-being:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaboration and community are central to what we do. We foster moments for creativity, connection, and reflection, respecting the need for work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Projects with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We partner with clients to use design as a means of realising their purpose and making a positive impact. We work &#39;upstream,&#39; from defining the problem, designing possible solutions, and exploring what, why and how they might be brought to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£55,000 - 60,000 GBP, depending on experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some Previous Projects To Check Out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To get a flavour of the work we do in London, take a look at these case studies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/sage&quot;&gt;Climate action for SMBs&lt;/a&gt; – Designing a strategy and experience to help Sage’s SMB customers transition to net zero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/case-study/femsa&quot;&gt;Redefining retail with FEMSA&lt;/a&gt; – Designing Spin Premia, a digital loyalty experience connecting everyday shopping at OXXO with rewards and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/h-and-m&quot;&gt;Sustainable packaging system&lt;/a&gt; – Helping H&amp;amp;M increase their sustainability and growth, by designing and scaling a universal packaging system for all of their brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IDEO, we are committed to the work of advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion within our organisation and in the world. Our purpose of having disproportionate, world-changing impact through design is directly connected to our ability to bring many different perspectives to the table. This applies to our candidates, the people we hire, the clients and customers we serve, and the communities we learn from in our research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a human-centred organisation, we are committed to working with and designing for people of every race, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, socio-economic status, physical ability or attribute, religion, national origin, or political belief. We recognize that this commitment requires ongoing work and sustained attention, as well as adaptation to new insights and best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Requirements And Instructions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you identify with our values, are excited about great design, and would like to contribute to our community, we would love to see your CV, a cover letter and examples of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help protect what truly matters in our customers&#39; most critical environments by proactively identifying threats and improving how they are detected and addressed.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission Critical Security Engineer with a focus on Threat Hunting, you will be part of a dedicated customer team responsible for securing and continuously improving a complex, mission-critical application landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working alongside other engineers and security specialists, you will help ensure the environment remains as secure and resilient as possible. You combine a strong engineering foundation with a security mindset, taking ownership of security improvements and understanding how systems, applications, and infrastructure behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your specific focus will be on threat hunting and detection engineering. Using your in-depth knowledge of the customer&#39;s technology stack and application landscape, you will fine-tune existing detection use cases and develop new ones tailored to the environment. You will use our custom SIEM/SOAR-based Managed Detection and Response (MDR) platform to turn emerging threats and technical insights into actionable detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role bridges security engineering, detection engineering, and threat intelligence. You don&#39;t simply follow predefined playbooks. You understand system behavior, identify gaps, and develop practical solutions that strengthen the security of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat intelligence &amp;amp; continuous improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actively follow security developments, vulnerabilities, and threat intelligence and translate these into relevant hunts and detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify security risks and gaps in detection coverage and proactively propose improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your knowledge of the customer&#39;s application and infrastructure landscape to continuously strengthen its security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the evolution of the team&#39;s security monitoring and detection strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate findings into clear, actionable communication for engineers, customer stakeholders, and security specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to security advisories and share relevant threats across the customer team and wider organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with engineers to understand system behavior and validate detection strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with the customer&#39;s Security Operations Center (SOC) to align security monitoring, threat detection, and response activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help establish and improve integrations with the customer&#39;s SIEM/SOAR platform, including the forwarding of relevant logs and security telemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection engineering &amp;amp; threat hunting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and continuously improve detection use cases based on emerging threats and observed behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate threat scenarios and security insights into actionable detection logic tailored to the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proactively perform threat hunting across the application and infrastructure landscape to identify abnormal or suspicious patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analyze logs and telemetry data to uncover behaviors that are not yet covered by existing detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your understanding of the customer&#39;s technology stack to distinguish normal from potentially malicious behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use case development &amp;amp; response design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define what should happen when detections trigger, including response actions, automation, and escalation paths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuously refine detection logic to improve quality, relevance, and signal-to-noise ratio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and fine-tune custom detection scenarios based on the specific characteristics and security requirements of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage our custom SIEM/SOAR-based MDR platform to implement detections and analyze data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with platform and automation engineers to improve integrations and detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply engineering and automation practices to ensure detection solutions are scalable, reliable, and maintainable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines solid engineering fundamentals with a strong interest in security and is motivated to move towards or deepen their expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t necessarily need to be an experienced threat hunter already. What matters is your ability to understand complex systems, recognize unusual behavior, and translate technical insights into practical security improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid engineering fundamentals, including Linux, networking, and infrastructure behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, or similar platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with CI/CD, Git, and configuration management or infrastructure-as-code tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong automation mindset and the ability to translate problems into scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with logs and telemetry to analyze system behavior and investigate technical issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Python and/or Bash scripting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with SIEM or log analytics platforms such as OpenSearch, Elastic, Splunk, or Microsoft Sentinel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of security principles, including threat detection and response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to distinguish normal from abnormal system behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analytical, curious, and driven to understand how systems and threats behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ownership mindset, with responsibility for security quality and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication skills to translate technical findings into actionable insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to connect business and customer context to technical security solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with threat hunting, detection engineering, or advanced SOC operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience developing or improving detection use cases and security monitoring rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with SOAR or security automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep knowledge of Microsoft Entra ID, Azure, and other Microsoft cloud services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with threat intelligence frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience integrating SIEM/SOAR platforms or forwarding security telemetry between different environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ Who are you?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an engineer with a strong interest in security, driven to understand how systems behave and how threats manifest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t follow playbooks blindly. You want to understand why detections exist, how systems interact, and where security can be improved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You combine analytical thinking with a hands-on mindset and enjoy working with complex applications, infrastructure, and data. You are curious, proactive, and take ownership of the quality of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also enjoy being part of a customer team where security is a shared responsibility. You work closely with fellow engineers and security specialists, communicate clearly with stakeholders, and contribute to keeping the entire environment secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What can you expect?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis, you&#39;ll join a community of engineers with an awesome combination of exceptionally high security standards, an infatuation with automation, and the power to make a positive, sustainable impact on customers&#39; business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work within a dedicated customer team where engineers and security specialists jointly take responsibility for the security and reliability of mission-critical environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of our customer engagements, there is no pressure on (billable) hours; we focus on quality and impact or how we like to call it:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;freedom &amp;amp; responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;. You know best how to deliver the most value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be embedded in a company committed to helping colleagues grow as people and professionals through training, knowledge sharing, mentoring, and good old-fashioned fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are high-quality workspaces, and we go way beyond what is expected. We have productive equipment, good food and drinks, team outings, family days, labs to experiment with innovative technologies, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re active in relevant tech communities, attending and organizing meetups and conferences, and we organize internal knowledge-sharing events where Tech Leads play an important role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re an engineer in the Netherlands with a strong interest in security and want to help secure mission-critical environments while developing or deepening your expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
